## Session 29 summary

**Infrastructure (fixed, reboot-stable):** test1 was unreachable — root cause was dynamic dnsmasq leases (test1 had drifted to .114). Added `dhcp-host` reservations (test1=.186, test2=.182) in `/etc/dnsmasq.d/lab.conf`; cluster now reboot-stable. Added reusable `scripts/vm_console_type.py` for VGA-console recovery. Recorded in `env-test1-dhcp-reservation-fix-sess29`.

**Root cause (PROVEN, RULE 4):** Built a `P29-DATAWRITE` write-side detector that proved the durable dirent loss is `xfsaild` async-flushing **stale dir DATA/leaf blocks across DLM tenure boundaries while EX-held** (the sess65 async-writeback gap). The RMW base is stale because at re-acquire the cached dir block is pin-only (`pinned, !dirty, !in_ail, DONE`) and both the read-hook and the modify-path clean-only evict refuse to refresh a pinned buffer (can't clear XBF_DONE → corruption). Two faces: data-block dirent loss + leaf-hash hole. Recorded in `sess29-PROVEN-root-xfsaild-stale-dirblock-flush-at-EX`.

**Approaches tested:**
- `dir_merge=1` (union-merge) **fixes the DATA face** (readdir 187→200) but causes `rc=-110` DLM-timeout shutdown — confirmed the **merge-while-holding-EX class is dead** (sess17/18/29). Once-per-tenure variant also timed out.
- Datascan `cmpresult` reset added (real lookup-skip bug, keep).

**Path forward (GPT-5.5 design, recorded in `sess29-GPT-design-tenure-local-poison-purge-at-NL`):** epoch-driven **tenure-local buffer invalidation** — poison pin-only stale dir buffers at release, **purge them at NL** (after demote, before next acquire) where waiting doesn't block a peer, and gate re-acquire on purge completion so a stale buffer is **never** an RMW base or xfsaild target. This avoids extending the EX hold (no peer timeout) and never clears XBF_DONE on a pinned buffer. Much machinery exists (release stale loop, acquire drain, gen/incarn stamps, chokepoint guard) — the new piece is poison + purge-at-NL + acquire gate.

**Build at relay:** `AB435ACC` (baseline + P29 detector + inert once-per-tenure merge [dir_merge default OFF] + datascan cmpresult fix). Next session: implement the GPT tenure-local-poison design; reboot cluster before each run (a shutdown leaves `/dev/sda` busy → prep fails).

